t:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":55260,"output_tokens":4182,"requests":6}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the Approach rationale: some producers (RunRequest default target={} at runner.py:180; the code-review gate at shim.py:96) omit ticket_ids entirely, so `.get(\"ticket_ids\")` can return None — keep the `else None` guard covering BOTH the empty-list and missing-key cases (the plan's fix already does; just fix the wrong 'never omit the key' claim).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1277,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["runner.py:180: `target={} if target is None else target` — a live missing-key path","code_review/shim.py:96: `target={\"kind\": \"code\", \"commits\": [base, head], \"files\": changed_files}` — a producer that omits ticket_ids entirely, flowing through findings.py finalize","Plan's own Testing already pins 'a request whose target omits ticket_ids entirely also yields ticket=None' — contradicting the Approach's 'never omit the key' claim"],"finding":"The plan's load-bearing rationale that 'producers always write ticket_ids as a list (possibly empty), never omit the key, so the empty-list case is the real path to handle, not a missing key' is factually wrong: RunRequest defaults target to {} (runner.py:180) and the code-review gate producer writes target={'kind':'code','commits':...,'files':...} with no ticket_ids key at all (code_review/shim.py:96 -> findings.py:235). The proposed fix's `else None` branch still handles this safely, so the mechanism is correct, but the rationale (and the plan's claim that the missing-key case is not a real path) is false and could mislead the implementer into dropping the missing-key guard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8fbf51371ced7767","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'producers always write ticket_ids as a list (possibly empty), never omit the key'","norm_id":"n5e19d97d8ed86331","priority":0.4723,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Code-review gate run (code target) produces a usage row","Any RunRequest built with target=None"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace the 'never omit the key' sentence with: 'most producers write ticket_ids as a list (possibly empty), but some targets omit it entirely (RunRequest default target={}, and the code-review gate\\'s code target), so `.get(\"ticket_ids\")` may return None or a list; the `ticket_ids[0] if ticket_ids else None` guard covers both.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add src/rebar/llm/spec_scan.py (target={..., \"ticket_ids\": [...]}, lines 128 and 139) to the enumerated set of target producers, and confirm its empty-ticket_ids batches are covered by the empty-list attribution path.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.425,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'every producer of target writes the plural key ticket_ids (src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py and src/rebar/llm/operations.py)'","spec_scan.py:128 `target={\"kind\": \"spec_scan\", \"ticket_ids\": [t.get(\"ticket_id\") for t in batch]}` inside RunRequest(...) then selected.run(req)","spec_scan.py:139 also builds `target={\"kind\": \"spec_scan\", \"ticket_ids\": epic_ids}`","The record() call sites at runner.py:682/756 read this same target for any RunRequest, spec_scan included"],"finding":"The plan enumerates only runs.py and operations.py as producers of target, but src/rebar/llm/spec_scan.py is a third producer that also builds target={\"kind\": \"spec_scan\", \"ticket_ids\": [...]} and feeds it through RunRequest into the same runner record() path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa37b1f865eb068ab","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem and Scope sections ('src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py and src/rebar/llm/operations.py')","norm_id":"nb2ec66e1cc07cc68","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An epic bug-screen / spec-scan run: its usage rows also currently lose the ticket and are fixed by the same edit, so spec_scan should be listed as a benefiting producer and its empty-ticket_ids path considered."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In the Context/Problem and Scope sections, list spec_scan.py alongside runs.py and operations.py as a producer that writes ticket_ids, noting it too benefits from the fix and can emit an empty ticket_ids list.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altit